CLASSIFICATION RULES:
- Use only the supplied candidate profile and job fields.
- Use "unknown" when employment type, IR35 status, or working pattern is not explicit.
- Do not assume work authorization, sponsorship, clearance, relocation, location eligibility, or outside-IR35 status.
- Keep match score components and evidence-based reasons separate.
- Every match reason must map to a supplied candidate-profile or job field.
- Do not add candidate metrics or qualifications.

For each job in the input array, classify it and provide a match score against this candidate profile.

USER:
Classify each job posting below. For each job, return:
- employment_type: one of "contract" | "permanent" | "fixed_term" | "part_time" | "freelance" | "unknown"
- ir35_status: one of "outside" | "inside" | "not_applicable" | "unknown"
- working_pattern: one of "remote" | "hybrid" | "onsite" | "unknown"
- seniority: one of "junior" | "mid" | "senior" | "lead" | "principal" | "head" | "director" | null
- match_score: integer 0-100 (how well this job matches the candidate profile above)
  - 85-100: Excellent fit — primary role, right rate, outside IR35, remote/hybrid
  - 70-84: Good fit — primary or secondary role, suitable rate
  - 50-69: Moderate fit — adjacent role or unclear details
  - 0-49: Poor fit — wrong seniority, wrong sector, permanent only, or very low rate
- match_reasons: array of up to 3 short strings explaining the score (e.g. "Cloud Architect — primary target role")
- red_flags: array of short strings for concerns (e.g. "Inside IR35", "Very low rate for seniority") — empty array if none

Return ONLY a JSON object with key "jobs" containing an array of results in the same order as input. Each result must include the original "id" field.

